  - *Tamil Bhakti Canons:* *Nalayira Divyaprabandham* = 4,000 hymns of 12 Alvars (*Tamil Veda*); *Tevaram* = hymns of Appar, Sambandar, Sundarar (Nayanars).
  - *Female Saints:* *Andal* (bridal love for Vishnu); *Karaikkal Ammaiyar* (skeletal ascetic demoness / *pey* for Shiva); *Akka Mahadevi* (naked ascetic for Shiva / Chennamallikarjuna); *Mirabai* (bridal devotion to Giridhar Gopal / disciple of untouchable Raidas).
  - *Virashaiva Radicalism:* Led by *Basavanna* in 12th c. Karnataka; *silver linga box* worn on shoulder; *buried* sitting (no cremation); rejected *rebirth* & caste; Kannada *Vachanas*.
  - *Five Chishti Saints (Sequence):* (1) Muinuddin Chishti (Ajmer), (2) Bakhtiyar Kaki (Delhi), (3) Baba Farid (Ajodhan), (4) Nizamuddin Auliya (Delhi), (5) Nasiruddin Chiragh-i Dehli.
  - *Chishti Practices:* *Khanqah* (hospice), *Langar* (kitchen), *Sama'* (musical audition / Qawwali), *Ziyarat* (pilgrimage), *Urs* (death anniversary / union).
  - *Northern Sants:* *Kabir* (weaver of Varanasi, *Ulatbansi*, *Bijak*); *Guru Nanak* (*Nirankar*, *Shabad*, *Langar*, *Adi Granth* in 1604 by Arjan, *Khalsa* in 1699 by Gobind Singh with 5 Ks).
  - *Regional Traditions:* *Shankaradeva* (Assam, *Sattras*, *Namghars*); *Varkaris* of Maharashtra (Pandharpur / Vithoba; Jnaneshwar, Namdev, Tukaram).
]

