#cheatsheet-box(title: "Master Strategy Cheatsheet — Bhakti-Sufi Traditions")[
  - *Nirguna vs Saguna:*
    - *Nirguna:* Formless, abstract, unconditioned Supreme Reality; no idols, no avatars, no temple rites (Kabir, Guru Nanak, Baba Farid, Raidas).
    - *Saguna:* Manifest personal deity with specific attributes, names, and visual iconographies (Alvars, Nayanars, Mirabai, Chaitanya, Tulsidas, Surdas).
  - *Zimmi & Jizya Mechanism:* Non-Muslim subjects under the Delhi Sultanate paid the *Jizya* poll tax to secure internal autonomy, customary law management, and state military protection.
  - *Sufi Lineage Vocabulary:* *Shaikh / Pir / Murshid* (spiritual guide), *Murid* (disciple), *Khalifa* (designated successor), *Khanqah* (hospice community), *Malfuzat* (conversations of saints).
  - *Akbar's Chishti Patronage:* Visited Ajmer shrine *14 times*, walked on foot, celebrated son Jahangir's birth via Shaikh Salim Chishti at Fatehpur Sikri.
  - *Sikh Scriptural Progression:* *Adi Granth* compiled 1604 by Guru Arjan -> Expanded with 9th Guru Tegh Bahadur's hymns -> Proclaimed *Guru Granth Sahib* in 1708.
]

#exception-box(title: "The Seven Fatal CUET Traps")[
  1. *Trap 1 (Jagannatha's Origin):* Assuming Jagannatha was always a classical Vedic deity. He began as an indigenous *tribal wooden deity* assimilated into Vishnu.
  2. *Trap 2 (Alvar vs Nayanar Focus):* Reversing the deities. *Alvars* were devoted to *Vishnu*; *Nayanars* were devoted to *Shiva*.
  3. *Trap 3 (Lingayat Cremation Myth):* Believing Lingayats practiced Hindu cremation. They *buried* their dead in sitting posture and rejected rebirth and funeral purifications.
  4. *Trap 4 (Chishti Royal Titles):* Thinking Chishti saints accepted high government posts. They strictly *refused* court offices and titles, preserving spiritual independence.
  5. *Trap 5 (Kabir's Authorship):* Assuming Kabir wrote manuscripts himself. His verses were oral utterances compiled posthumously in *Bijak*, *Kabir Granthavali*, and *Adi Granth*.
  6. *Trap 6 (Sikh Khalsa Year):* Confusing 1604 with 1699. *Adi Granth* was compiled in *1604*; the *Khalsa* was created in *1699* by Guru Gobind Singh.
  7. *Trap 7 (Mirabai's Preceptor):* Assuming Mirabai had a royal Brahmana guru. Her chosen spiritual preceptor was *Raidas*, an untouchable leather-worker.
]

